+# Key v2, amendment 1 (a1), revision 1
+
+Status: S3 fixed by the owner 2026-11-18 as S3-out; S1, S2, ND, N1, C1, K1
+accepted as drafted. Revision 1 (same day, before any further reading) closes
+two gaps that `amendment_options/OPTIONS.md` found in the patch as received
+(choice 1: S2 read literally removes T14's `sigma, basis`; choice 2: S1(b) read
+literally collects the 14 fields of the `proposal` record for T01). Revision 1
+is in force when the owner applies it; its sha256 is then recorded in
+`PREREG.md` (dated section "Key v2, amendment 1").
+`key_v2.json` is unchanged; the amended key is `scoring/key_v2_a1.json`.
+
+Drafted by: the Claude-v2-A model, AFTER it had seen key v2 and its own score,
+and (for revision 1) after it had seen `amendment_options/`, which scores that
+reading under candidate keys. The drafter is not independent of the key or of a
+reader. The safeguard is procedural: each change below follows from a rule
+stated in section 1, each rule is applied to all 15 terms in section 2
+(including the terms where it moves the key AWAY from both Claude readings),
+and the text is fixed and hashed before a reader of another family reads.
+
+Scope: `slots_specific` rules, one scorer normalization, one scorer report
+addition. The brief, the packet, the grouping key and the `slots_carried` key
+lists are NOT changed. v2 readers stay poolable.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Rules
+
+```text
+S1  COLLECT  A name enters slots_specific if the source gives it by one of:
+             (a) a parameter of a constructor / function written for this term only
+             (b) a field of THIS TERM'S OWN RECORD -- the record whose status / kind /
+                 verdict / state value is this term -- where that record's shape is
+                 built only on this term's path                          [revised R-b]
+             (c) a field a source rule REQUIRES for this status
+                 (raises / refuses without it, or a spec table marks it "required")
+             (d) a documented key list or notation parameter for this term
+             Not opened under (b): another record built alongside the term's own
+             record, or held in one of its fields. Such a record is collected, if
+             at all, for the term whose own record it is.               [revised R-b]
+
+S2  EXCLUDE  Remove a collected name when it is not this term's alone, tested the
+             same way it was collected:                                 [revised R-a]
+             - a name collected by (a), (b) or (d) (because a record or signature
+               HAS it) is removed if every other status sharing that record or
+               constructor also has it. Presence counts, not value: a key present on
+               every record of a kind is shared even when it is None on the other
+               paths.
+             - a name collected by (c) (because a rule REQUIRES it) is removed if
+               every other status sharing that record also requires it. A field
+               every record has, but only this status requires, stays.
+             (e.g. `reason` where the rule is "every non-verdict token needs one":
+             removed under both tests)
+
+S3  ATTRS    S3-out (decided: a slot is an input degree of freedom; derived
+             attributes carry no new information)
+             Only S1(a), (c), (d) names and declared class / record fields count.
+             An attribute computed after construction from the parameters
+             (covers_effect; typed / untyped split out of triggers) is filled by
+             nothing: it is a function of slots already counted, and counting it
+             would count the same information twice.
+  [STRUCK]   S3-in   an attribute set by the source on this term's record only
+  [STRUCK]           (not a parameter) is collected under S1(b)
+             Counter-evidence considered (revision 1): tokens.py 17-18, "Reading
+             added here: `covers_effect` (limit <= effect size) is reported on a
+             scoped absence. It refuses nothing; the spec requires the fields, not
+             the comparison." The source reports covers_effect on this term. S3-out
+             keeps it out because the same sentence says it is a comparison of two
+             slots already counted, which nothing fills.
+
+ND  TEST     After S1-S3, if the sources still support two different lists,
+             the list is undetermined (null), as PREREG v2 already defines n/d.
+
+N1  SCORER   Before comparing names, strip one pair of surrounding `<` `>` and
+             surrounding backticks. Nothing else changes (the scorer's existing
+             strip + lowercase is kept; underscores and spaces are kept).
+
+C1  SCORER   For each determined list, beside equal / differ, report the set
+             relation: equal | reader-superset | reader-subset | overlap | disjoint.
+             For a superset, list the extras. Reported beside the existing
+             numbers; it replaces none of them and adds no combined score.
+
+K1  CLARIFY  `slots_carried` "instance fields, checked by running it" means
+             vars(instance): class attributes (e.g. ExpiryTrigger.is_exit) are
+             not instance fields. No list changes under K1.
+```
+
+Why R-a and R-b, from the brief (READER_BRIEF.md line 22): `slots_specific` is
+"the named fields or parameters the source ties to this term and to no other
+term. Examples: a class written for the term, the parameters of a function or
+notation written for it, a documented key list for it, or a rule that says this
+status needs certain fields. Not fields that every term sharing a record has."
+
+- R-a. The brief collects by two different kinds of tie: a record that HAS a
+  field, and a rule that REQUIRES one. A single presence test applied to a
+  requirement-collected name always removes it (every namedtuple status has
+  every field), which would make the brief's own fourth example empty by
+  construction. So each name is tested for exclusivity by the tie it was
+  collected under.
+- R-b. The brief's examples are things written FOR the term. The `proposal`
+  record (numcheck `_identity_candidate`) is written for an identity candidate:
+  it carries its own `status` (PROPOSED / DERIVED), and the check's header says
+  "The check's own verdict is not changed". The TAF section record
+  `{error, exception_type, missing_path}` is the module's report section, built
+  beside the coverage entry, not the entry itself. Neither is the term's own
+  record. Applying one rule to both keeps T01 and T10 consistent with each
+  other; the patch as received opened one (T10) and not the other (T01).
+
